---
layout: layouts/product.njk
title: "VoiceTel SDN appliance"
description: "A small on-prem VoiceTel SDN appliance creates a secure tunnel for SIP traversal through NAT, ALG, UDP timer, and firewall constraints."
---
{%- from "partials/v2/macros.njk" import arrow %}

<script type="application/ld+json">
{
	"@context": "https://schema.org",
	"@type": "Service",
	"serviceType": "On-premises SIP traversal appliance",
	"name": "VoiceTel SDN appliance",
	"provider": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "{{ site.brand }}", "url": "{{ site.url }}" },
	"areaServed": ["US", "CA"],
	"url": "{{ site.url }}/sdn/",
	"description": "An on-prem appliance that establishes a secure tunnel from the customer LAN to VoiceTel, removing the need for ALG, NAT, UDP timer, and firewall tuning for SIP. Supports Asterisk, FreePBX, FreeSWITCH, and FusionPBX."
}
</script>

<section class="hero hero--page" aria-labelledby="hero-heading">
	<div class="hero__bg" aria-hidden="true"></div>
	<div class="container hero__inner">
		<div class="hero__copy">
			<p class="eyebrow">SDN appliance</p>
			<h1 id="hero-heading">A small appliance for difficult SIP networks.</h1>
			<p class="lede">The VoiceTel SDN appliance sits inside the customer LAN and establishes a secure tunnel to VoiceTel, helping PBX registrations and media flows avoid common NAT, ALG, UDP timer, and firewall problems.</p>
			<div class="cta-row">
				<a class="btn btn--primary btn--lg" href="/signup/">Try for free {{ arrow(14) }}</a>
				<a class="btn btn--ghost btn--lg" href="/sdn/technical-specification/">Technical specification</a>
			</div>
		</div>
		<div class="hero__visual">
			{%- set diagram = {
				title: "Your LAN to the SDN appliance to VoiceTel core",
				nodes: [
					{ label: "Your LAN", value: "PBX + phones", meta: "10.0.0.0/24" },
					{ label: "SDN appliance", value: "Raspberry Pi", meta: "sdn-08c4", accent: true },
					{ label: "VoiceTel core", value: "NYC POP", meta: "TLS 1.3 tunnel" }
				],
				links: [{}, { accent: true }],
				meta: [
					{ k: "Uplink", v: ":443 outbound" },
					{ k: "Firewall", v: "no routing changes" },
					{ k: "Media", v: "SIP + RTP inside" }
				]
			} %}
			{% include "partials/v2/diagram.njk" %}
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<section class="section section--tint" id="solves" aria-labelledby="solves-heading">
	<div class="container">
		<div class="row">
			<div class="row__text">
				<p class="eyebrow">What it solves</p>
				<h2 id="solves-heading">No audio, flapping registrations, firewall friction, and blind spots.</h2>
				<p class="lede">The appliance gives VoiceTel a controlled path for signaling and media, keeps local PBX registration behavior stable, reduces the need for broad inbound SIP and RTP exposure at the customer edge, and gives support a clear demarcation point.</p>
				<div class="cta-row">
					<a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/sdn/technical-specification/">Technical specification</a>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="row__visual">
				<figure class="photo-card">
					<img src="/assets/img/sdn-rpi.jpg" alt="VoiceTel SDN appliance, a small Raspberry Pi-form-factor device" width="600" height="401" loading="lazy">
					<figcaption>The VoiceTel SDN appliance, compact enough to deploy alongside any PBX or SBC.</figcaption>
				</figure>
			</div>
		</div>

		<h3 class="subsection-heading">Problems it removes</h3>
		{%- set featureHeading = "h4" %}
		{%- set features = [
			{ icon: "broadcast-pin", title: "No audio or one-way audio", body: "Media-path issues often come from NAT, firewall, or RTP pinhole behavior. The appliance gives VoiceTel a controlled path." },
			{ icon: "activity", title: "Registration instability", body: "Keep local PBX registration behavior stable while the appliance handles the upstream secure path." },
			{ icon: "shield-check", title: "Firewall policy friction", body: "Reduce the need to open broad inbound SIP and RTP exposure at the customer edge." },
			{ icon: "headset", title: "Support visibility", body: "Give support a clearer demarcation point for diagnosing LAN, tunnel, SIP, and media behavior." }
		] %}
		{% include "partials/v2/feature-grid.njk" %}
	</div>
</section>

<section class="section section--white" id="integrations" aria-labelledby="integrations-heading">
	<div class="container">
		<div class="row row--reverse">
			<div class="row__text">
				<p class="eyebrow">Integrations</p>
				<h2 id="integrations-heading">PBX-agnostic, with any standards-compliant SIP endpoint.</h2>
				<p class="lede">Configuration guides cover FreePBX, FusionPBX, and 3CX, with SBC interop notes for Asterisk, FreeSWITCH, Cisco CUBE, and AudioCodes.</p>
				<div class="cta-row">
					<a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/support/voice/">All voice guides</a>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="row__visual">
				{%- set docs = [
					{ icon: "diagram-3", title: "FreePBX", meta: "PBX", href: "/support/voice/pbx/freepbx/" },
					{ icon: "diagram-3", title: "FusionPBX", meta: "PBX", href: "/support/voice/pbx/fusionpbx/" },
					{ icon: "diagram-3", title: "3CX", meta: "PBX", href: "/support/voice/pbx/3cx/" },
					{ icon: "hdd-stack", title: "Asterisk", meta: "SBC", href: "/support/voice/sbc/asterisk/" },
					{ icon: "hdd-stack", title: "FreeSWITCH", meta: "SBC", href: "/support/voice/sbc/freeswitch/" },
					{ icon: "hdd-stack", title: "Cisco CUBE", meta: "SBC", href: "/support/voice/sbc/cisco-cube/" },
					{ icon: "hdd-stack", title: "AudioCodes", meta: "SBC", href: "/support/voice/sbc/audiocodes/" }
				] %}
				{% include "partials/v2/docs-list.njk" %}
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<section class="section section--tint" id="resellers" aria-labelledby="resellers-heading">
	<div class="container">
		<div class="row">
			<div class="row__text">
				<p class="eyebrow">For integrators and resellers</p>
				<h2 id="resellers-heading">Ship the appliance; the SIP problems stay behind the tunnel.</h2>
				<p class="lede">Ship the appliance to the customer's office. Their SIP problems disappear behind a controlled tunnel to VoiceTel, with no firewall reconfiguration, no broad inbound exposure, and no multi-day diagnosis cycles. You bill the customer; we bill you per appliance per month.</p>
				<div class="cta-row">
					<a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/integrators/">Partner with VoiceTel</a>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="row__visual">
				{%- set rates = [
					{ name: "SDN appliance", unit: "/ appliance / month", id: "sdn", star: true }
				] %}
				{%- set rateFootnote = "Volume discounts bring the rate down toward $5 at scale. Billed alongside your VoiceTel account; ships pre-configured for your tenant." %}
				{% include "partials/v2/price-table.njk" %}
			</div>
		</div>

		<div class="cta-band">
			<div class="cta-band__text">
				<h3 class="cta-band__title">Ready to deploy?</h3>
				<p class="cta-band__body">A very small price to pay for total business continuity.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="cta-band__actions cta-row">
				<a class="btn btn--primary" href="/signup/">Sign up {{ arrow(14) }}</a>
				<a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/pricing/#sdn">See pricing</a>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>
